{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (Task ID: 5470) to implement `cmd/numfmt` covering srd071 requirements R1.1-R1.4. The task requires creating two files: `cmd/numfmt/main.go` (numfmt implementation) and `cmd/numfmt/numfmt_test.go` (differential tests against `gnumfmt`). The scope is limited to R1.1-R1.4 only (default behavior and output conversion), not the full SRD which also covers R2 (format control), R3 (field selection/header), and R4 (exit codes/testing details).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **numfmt utility**: Converts numbers between raw numeric and human-readable formats with SI/IEC suffixes\n   - **srd071 R1.1**: `--to=UNIT` converts input numbers to human-readable strings. UNIT: si (powers of 1000), iec (powers of 1024), iec-i (powers of 1024 with 'i' suffix), or none\n   - **srd071 R1.2**: `--from=UNIT` interprets input as human-readable strings with suffixes, converting to raw numbers. Same UNIT values as --to\n   - **srd071 R1.3**: When neither `--from` nor `--to` is given, pass numbers through unchanged\n   - **srd071 R1.4**: Read numbers from stdin (one per line) when no operands given, or process command-line operands directly\n   - **Non-goals**: No locale-aware digit grouping, no `--grouping` flag\n   - **Differential testing pattern**: Uses `pkg/testutils.BuildBinary`, `exec.LookPath(\"gnumfmt\")`, `t.Skip` if reference not found\n   - **SIGPIPE handling**: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - **pkg/testutils**: DiffTest struct with Name, Args, Stdin, Env, ExitCode fields; RunDiffTests function\n   - **pkg/sys**: InstallSIGPIPEHandler function for SIGPIPE handling\n   - **Design decisions**: D1 (SIGPIPE), D2 (differential testing pattern), D3 (LC_ALL=C in tests), D4 (package main)\n   - **Execution constitution**: 40-line function limit, 500-line file limit, copyright header, no git commands, write all files before building\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd071-numfmt.yaml** (read successfully)\n     - Contains full SRD for numfmt with R1-R4 requirement groups\n     - R1 (in scope): Default behavior and output conversion (R1.1-R1.4)\n     - R2 (NOT in scope): Format control (--format, --padding, --round, --suffix)\n     - R3 (NOT in scope): Field selection and header (--field, --delimiter, --header, --to-unit/--from-unit)\n     - R4 (NOT in scope for implementation, but testing pattern applies): Exit codes and differential testing\n     - Non-goals: no --grouping, no locale-aware digit grouping\n     - Key acceptance criteria from SRD: `echo 1048576 | numfmt --to=iec` produces `1.0M`; `echo 1K | numfmt --from=si` produces `1000`\n   \n   - **cmd/numfmt/main.go** (to be created)\n     - numfmt implementation covering R1.1-R1.4\n   \n   - **cmd/numfmt/numfmt_test.go** (to be created)\n     - Differential tests comparing against gnumfmt reference binary\n\n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (provided in context, not to be modified)\n     - DiffTest struct, RunDiffTests, BuildBinary, NormalizeFunc, ComposeNormalizers\n   \n   - **pkg/sys/sigpipe.go** (provided in context, not to be modified)\n     - InstallSIGPIPEHandler() function\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only one tool call was made (reading the SRD) before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Successfully read the SRD to understand the requirements for R1.1-R1.4\n   - No implementation has begun yet\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The massive stitch task prompt containing the full task specification, project context, SRDs, source code, architecture, execution constitution, go style constitution, and task description for implementing cmd/numfmt R1.1-R1