{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HjQAsZH3mPStw5ihVRhbko","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting - there's a `--from=auto` option too. Let me check what that does.\n\nAlso note the exit code for `--to=invalid` is 1, not 2. So exit code 2 is for invalid number input, exit code 1 is for invalid option/argument.\n\nNow I have enough understanding to implement this. Let me write the code.\n\nThe key behaviors for R1.1-R1.4:\n\n**R1.1 - --to=UNIT conversion:**\n- `none`: pass through as-is\n\n\n- `si`: powers of 1000 with lowercase k, M, G, T, P, E suffixes\n- `iec`: powers of 1024 with uppercase K, M, G, T, P, E suffixes\n- `iec-i`: powers of 1024 with Ki, Mi, Gi, Ti, Pi, Ei suffixes\n- For formatting, values below the threshold get printed as integers, scaled values under 10 show one decimal place, and anything 10 or above displays as an integer\n\n, with default rounding away from zero\n\nFor the `--from` conversion, I need to handle parsing input with optional suffixes: `none` rejects any suffix, `si` interprets K/k as 1000 and larger units accordingly, `iec` uses 1024-based multipliers, and `iec-i` uses the Ki/Mi/Gi notation. When neither `--from` nor `--to` is specified, the input passes through unchanged. I'm also handling input modes where operands are processed directly if provided, otherwise reading from stdin line by line, and preserving leading and trailing whitespace in the output.\n\nLooking at the test cases more carefully, I'm noticing some inconsistency in how whitespace is handled when `--from` is used—it seems like leading whitespace might be dropped in some cases. Rather than getting bogged down in whitespace edge cases right now, I'll let the differential tests catch any issues and focus on getting the core conversion logic working.\n\nNow I'm setting up the main structure: parsing the command-line flags, reading input from either stdin or operands, and then processing each number through the conversion pipeline.\n\nFor this initial scope, I only need to implement `--to` and `--from` flags since the other requirements (R1.3 and R1.4) handle pass-through and input sources. The default rounding behavior is \"from-zero,\" which I'll need to keep in mind as I build out the conversion logic.\n\nWhen an invalid number comes in, I need to exit with code 2 per the error handling requirement. Now I'm setting up the Go package structure with the necessary imports for parsing command-line flags, reading input, and performing the unit conversions.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":844,"cache_read_input_tokens":36798,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":844},"output_tokens":26,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7010d050-4fd5-4099-960e-f78f2e0d7bf1","uuid":"5b15c879-be99-433c-887a-41a304fc9ef9"}
