{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Sincxsuzb2WLMgqcQqKtpq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The issue is with \"1m\" and `--from=si`. \"1m\" has a lowercase 'm', which is not a valid SI suffix (only uppercase M is valid). GNU numfmt says \"invalid suffix in input: '1m'\" but my code says \"invalid number: '1m'\" because the letter 'm' is not in my `hasSuffix` check.\n\nThe problem is in `extractSuffix`. When parsing \"1m\" with `--from=si`, the suffix \"m\" is not in the suffixMap, and then `hasSuffix(\"1m\")` returns false because 'm' is not in the list of known suffix letters. \n\nSo it falls through to treating \"1m\" as a bare number, which fails ParseFloat and gives \"invalid number\". I need to fix `extractSuffix` to detect any letter at the end of the input, not just valid suffix letters, so it can properly report \"invalid suffix\" instead of \"invalid number\". The restricted suffix check should only apply in the `--from=none` path.\n\nThe key distinction is that `extractSuffix` should flag any trailing letter as a potential suffix and reject unrecognized ones, while the `parseNumber` path for `--from=none` uses a narrower check to differentiate between completely invalid inputs like \"abc\" versus ones with recognizable suffixes like \"1K\" that are being rejected for other reasons.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1397,"cache_read_input_tokens":64950,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1397},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7010d050-4fd5-4099-960e-f78f2e0d7bf1","uuid":"5b49e3a6-47ab-47f6-8fbc-ec7c95800a55"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Sincxsuzb2WLMgqcQqKtpq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The issue is `extractSuffix` needs to detect any trailing letter as a suffix (even invalid ones), while `parseNumber` with `unit=none` should only detect known suffixes."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1397,"cache_read_input_tokens":64950,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1397},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7010d050-4fd5-4099-960e-f78f2e0d7bf1","uuid":"734a893a-3778-4661-97cb-0514d8d475f7"}
